        }
      ],
      "passed": true,
      "answer": "Based on the provided documents, Transformers replaced RNNs for the following reasons:\n\n1. **Parallelisation and Training Speed:** RNNs read sequences one token at a time, making training slow and difficult to parallelise. In contrast, Transformers process all tokens in a sequence simultaneously, which is well-suited for GPUs (*transformers_guide.txt*).\n2. **Long-range Relationships:** Transformers handle long-range relationships better because any token can attend directly to any other token, regardless of the distance between them (*transformers_guide.txt*).",
      "seconds": 2.0398051000083797,
